.TITLE "chkdsk"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Checks the file system and file system metadata of a volume for logical and physical errors. It provides a status report and can fix issues to ensure __disk integrity__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**chkdsk**
Checks the current drive and displays a status report.
> 

**chkdsk C:**
Checks the specified drive for errors.
> __C:__ the target drive letter

**chkdsk /f**
Fixes errors on the disk.
> __/f__ fix flag

**chkdsk /r**
Locates bad sectors and recovers readable information.
> __/r__ recover flag

**chkdsk /x**
Forces the volume to dismount first if necessary.
> __/x__ dismount flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Running __chkdsk /f__ often requires a system restart if the target drive is currently in use. Regularly checking your disks helps prevent data loss caused by file system corruption.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
